---
// What the newest pre-release of 3.0 gives now ("Presenting v3" in
// AGENTS.md): the measured change against the 2.x release that the check
// before its tag compared it with, then what a configuration or script can
// use in it. Everything here is in the release; the planned parts are in
// PlannedUseCases.astro, after the example and the trial.
//
// The numbers come from the report in src/data/ (lib/perf-report.mjs), with
// their month and method beside them (docs/proposals/site.md, Q8), and
// check-home.mjs compares them with it. The release named here is the head
// of that report, and the build stops when its tag is not in the repository.
import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';
import path from 'node:path';
import { measuredMonth, readPerfReport } from '../../scripts/lib/perf-report.mjs';
import { repoDir } from '../../scripts/lib/site.mjs';
const ja = Astro.props.lang === 'ja';
const prefix = ja ? '/ja' : '';
const report = readPerfReport(path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'src/data/perf-v3.0.0-alpha.1.txt'));
const tags = execFileSync('git', ['-C', repoDir, 'tag', '--list', 'v*'], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\n');
for (const tag of [report.base.tag, report.head.tag]) {
  if (!tags.includes(tag)) throw new Error(`V3Now: the tag ${tag} of the perf report is not in the repository; fetch the tags before building`);
}
const release = report.head.version;
const base = report.base.version;
const releaseUrl = `https://github.com/matsumotory/ngx_mruby/releases/tag/${report.head.tag}`;
const month = measuredMonth(report, ja ? 'ja' : 'en');
const fewer = report.rows.filter((r) => r.head < r.base);
const more = report.rows.filter((r) => r.head > r.base);
// The rows of the table, in the order of the release's text: the three
// largest decreases that it names, and every row that rose.
const SHOWN = [
  ['headers', 'ヘッダを読んで設定する', 'Read and set headers'],
  ['sub_request', 'サブリクエスト', 'Subrequest'],
  ['hello', 'helloを返す', 'Handler that returns hello'],
  ['filter', '出力ボディフィルター', 'Output body filter'],
];
const rows = SHOWN.map(([scenario, jaName, enName]) => {
  const row = report.rows.find((r) => r.scenario === scenario);
  if (!row) throw new Error(`V3Now: no row ${scenario} in the perf report`);
  return { ...row, name: ja ? jaName : enName };
});
for (const row of more) {
  if (!rows.some((r) => r.scenario === row.scenario)) throw new Error(`V3Now: the row ${row.scenario} rose and is not shown`);
}
const judgedRose = report.rows.filter((r) => r.judgedHead > r.judgedBase);
// The note says that these rows fell in the total and without GC alone.
for (const r of judgedRose) {
  if (!(r.head < r.base && r.noGcHead < r.noGcBase)) throw new Error(`V3Now: review the note on ${r.scenario}: it does not fall in the total and without GC`);
}
const units = report.units;
// The Japanese note says どちらも (both) of these rows.
if (judgedRose.length !== 2) throw new Error('V3Now: review the note on the judged figures: it names two scenarios');
const number = (n) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
const percent = (s) => s.replace('-', '−');
// Text in backquotes is code.
const parts = (text) => text.split('`');
const items = [
  {
    title: ['mruby 4.1.0-rc2を同梱', 'Bundles mruby 4.1.0-rc2'],
    text: [
      '同梱のmrubyが3.3.0から上がり、スクリプトでパターンマッチ(`case`/`in`)、ブロックの`it`、mruby 3.4から4.1までに増えたメソッドを使えます。',
      'The bundled mruby moves up from 3.3.0: scripts can use pattern matching (`case`/`in`), `it` in blocks and the methods that mruby 3.4 to 4.1 added.',
    ],
    href: ja ? '/ja/releases/v3.0.0/#同梱のmrubyが330から410-rc2になる561-678' : '/releases/v3.0.0/#the-bundled-mruby-is-410-rc2-instead-of-330-561-678',
    link: ['同梱のmrubyの変更と移行の注意', 'What changes with the bundled mruby, and what to do'],
  },
  {
    title: ['待つハンドラがどのフェーズでも同じように再開する', 'Handlers that wait behave the same in every phase'],
    text: [
      '`Nginx::Async.sleep`や`Nginx::Async::HTTP.sub_request`で待ったハンドラは、どのフェーズでも同じ形で再開し、リクエストを終えます。contentハンドラでも`sub_request`を使えます。',
      'A handler that waits in `Nginx::Async.sleep` or `Nginx::Async::HTTP.sub_request` resumes and ends the request in the same way in every phase. `sub_request` also works in content handlers.',
    ],
    href: prefix + '/concepts/async/',
    link: ['ブロックせずに待つ仕組み', 'How a handler waits without blocking'],
  },
  {
    title: ['効果の無い呼び出しは例外になる', 'Calls that would do nothing raise an error'],
    text: [
      'メソッドが、呼んだハンドラで効果を持たないときは、`RuntimeError`が発生します。誤りは無視されずに`error.log`に出ます。',
      'A method that has no effect in the handler that calls it raises a `RuntimeError`, so the mistake shows up in `error.log` instead of being ignored.',
    ],
    href: ja ? '/ja/releases/v3.0.0/#ハンドラで効果の無いメソッドはそのハンドラでruntimeerrorを出す826' : '/releases/v3.0.0/#methods-that-have-no-effect-in-a-handler-raise-a-runtimeerror-there-826',
    link: ['対象のメソッドとハンドラ', 'Which methods, in which handlers'],
  },
  {
    title: ['ハンドラの間で値を渡す', 'Pass values between handlers'],
    text: [
      '`Nginx::Request#store`で、1つのリクエストのハンドラの間で値を渡せます。`mruby_variable`で、スクリプトが代入するnginxの変数を宣言できます。',
      '`Nginx::Request#store` passes values between the handlers of one request, and `mruby_variable` declares nginx variables for scripts to assign.',
    ],
    href: prefix + '/concepts/lifetimes/',
    link: ['リクエストのデータを置く場所', 'Where the data of a request lives'],
  },
  {
    title: ['ヘッダがnginxのフィールドに入る', "Headers go into nginx's own fields"],
    text: [
      '`Nginx::Headers_out`で設定した`Content-Type`、`Location`、`Date`、`Server`はnginxのフィールドに入り、nginxのフィルターもその値を使います。`Nginx::Headers_in#[]=`で足したリクエストヘッダは、`proxy_pass`が認識します。',
      "`Content-Type`, `Location`, `Date` and `Server` set through `Nginx::Headers_out` go into nginx's own fields, which nginx's filters use. Request headers added with `Nginx::Headers_in#[]=` are recognized by `proxy_pass`.",
    ],
    href: prefix + '/reference/ruby/#nginxheaders_out-class',
    link: ['Nginx::Headers_outのリファレンス', 'Nginx::Headers_out reference'],
  },
  {
    title: ['モデルごとの振り分けを手元で動かす', 'Run model routing locally'],
    text: [
      '`examples/start`は、Docker Composeで、リクエストをモデルごとに2つのモックAPIへ振り分けるnginxを動かします。プロバイダーのAPIキーは不要です。',
      '`examples/start` uses Docker Compose to run an nginx that routes requests by model to two mock APIs. No provider API key is needed.',
    ],
    href: `https://github.com/matsumotory/ngx_mruby/blob/${report.head.tag}/examples/start/README.md`,
    link: [`${release}のexamples/startの手順`, `The steps of examples/start in ${release}`],
  },
];
---
<section class="v3-now" aria-labelledby="now-title">
  <div class="home-copy">
    <h2 id="now-title">{ja ? `${release}でいま使えるもの` : `What ${release} gives you now`}</h2>
    <p>{ja
      ? `${release}は、3.0の最初のプレリリースです。新しいコアが入っていて、ここに挙げるものはこのプレリリースにあります。AIゲートウェイの部品は、この後のプレリリースで足す予定です。下の「今後のユースケースと設計状況」で扱います。本番では安定版の2.x系を使ってください。`
      : `${release} is the first pre-release of 3.0. It brings the new core, and everything listed here is in it. The parts of an AI gateway are planned for later pre-releases; the future use cases below cover them. For production, use the stable 2.x line.`}</p>
    <p><a href={releaseUrl}>{ja ? `${release}のリリースノートと、更新前に確認する挙動の変更` : `Release notes of ${release}, with the behavior changes to read before upgrading`}</a></p>
  </div>
  <div class="now-measured">
    <h3>{ja ? `${month}に${base}と比べた、リクエストあたりの命令数` : `Instructions per request against ${base}, measured in ${month}`}</h3>
    <p>{ja
      ? `測った${report.rows.length}のシナリオのうち${fewer.length}で、${release}のnginxがリクエストごとに実行した命令の数は、${base}より少なくなりました。増えたのは${more.length}つです。値はcallgrindで数えた命令数で、実行時間ではありません。`
      : `In ${fewer.length} of the ${report.rows.length} measured scenarios, nginx with ${release} ran fewer instructions per request than with ${base}, and more in the ${more.length === 1 ? 'other one' : `other ${more.length}`}. These are instruction counts from callgrind, not times.`}</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">{ja ? 'シナリオ' : 'Scenario'}</th><th scope="col" class="num">{base}</th><th scope="col" class="num">{release}</th><th scope="col">{ja ? '変化' : 'Change'}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{rows.map((r) => <tr data-scenario={r.scenario}><th scope="row">{r.name}</th><td class="num">{number(r.base)}</td><td class="num">{number(r.head)}</td><td class="num">{percent(r.change)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="now-method">{ja
      ? <>測り方：<code>sh test/perf/compare.sh</code>で、callgrind上で動かしたnginxに、{number(report.warmup)}件のウォームアップの後、{number(report.n)}件のリクエストを送って命令数を数えました。{units.map((u) => <><code>{u}</code>だけは、リクエストではなくTCPセッションごとに数えています。</>)}arm64のMacのDockerで、Ubuntu 22.04のコンテナを使っています。表の値は、GCを含む命令数の合計です。</>
      : <>Method: <code>sh test/perf/compare.sh</code> ran nginx under callgrind, sent {number(report.warmup)} requests to warm up, then counted the instructions of {number(report.n)} requests{units.map((u) => <>; <code>{u}</code> counts per TCP session instead</>)}. It ran in an Ubuntu 22.04 container under Docker on an arm64 Mac. The table gives the total per request, GC included.</>}</p>
    <p class="now-method">{ja
      ? <>{report.rows.length}のシナリオすべての値は、<a href={report.source}>タグを付ける前の確認(#{report.number})</a>にあります。合否の判定には、GCと、mrubyの定数キャッシュにヒットしなかった定数の参照を除いた値を使います。この値では{judgedRose.map((r, i) => <>{i ? 'と' : ''}<code>{r.scenario}</code></>)}が増えています。差し引く参照が{base}にしかないためです。合計とGCだけを除いた値では、どちらも減っています。</>
      : <><a href={report.source}>#{report.number}, the check before the tag,</a> has all {report.rows.length} scenarios and the figures it gates on, which leave out GC and the constant lookups that missed mruby's cache. In those, {judgedRose.map((r, i) => <>{i ? ' and ' : ''}<code>{r.scenario}</code></>)} rose, because only {base} has such misses to leave out; their totals and their figures without GC alone fell.</>}</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="now-list">
    {items.map((item) => <li>
      <h3>{item.title[ja ? 0 : 1]}</h3>
      <p>{parts(item.text[ja ? 0 : 1]).map((part, i) => (i % 2 ? <code>{part}</code> : part))}</p>
      <a href={item.href}>{item.link[ja ? 0 : 1]}</a>
    </li>)}
  </ul>
</section>
